  the product in breach of ODbL.

OpenStreetMap tile servers
  Tiles served from tile.openstreetmap.org under the OSM Foundation Tile
  Usage Policy: https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/tiles/

  The policy covers a volunteer-funded service and forbids heavy or
  commercial bulk use. A launched product at real traffic is expected to
  move to a paid tile provider or self-host. Treat the current setup as
  suitable for development and demonstration only.

Nominatim (address search and reverse geocoding)
  Usage policy: https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/nominatim/

  Requires an identifying User-Agent or Referer on every request and no
  more than one request per second. The client honours both: a shared
  throttle enforces the rate limit across search and reverse lookups, and
  requests are debounced so typing does not fire one per keystroke.

  DO NOT raise that rate or remove the throttle. The public endpoint is
  also not intended for a production product at volume; a launch needs a
  self-hosted instance or a commercial geocoder.

